<title>ITALY: Italy offers 36.5 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</title>
<headline>Italy offers 36.5 trln lire of BOTs for sale.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian treasury said it was offering 36.5 trillion lire of short term bills (BOT), replacing 40.5 trillion lire of expiring paper.</p>
<p>A Treasury statement said it would offer:</p>
<p>* 11.0 trillion lire of three-month BOTs</p>
<p>* 11.5 trillion lire of six-month paper</p>
<p>* 14.0 trillion lire of one-year bills.</p>
<p>Subscriptions close at 1200 GMT on December 23.</p>
</text>
